CORE gcc-only
main.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion __builtin_isfinite\(big\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion !__builtin_isfinite\(nan\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
no body for callee
^warning: ignoring
--
A model `int __builtin_isfinite(double)' converted a long double argument
to double, so 1e400L became infinite.  The type checker now handles
__builtin_isfinite on the argument's own type, as GCC and Clang do.
